    "notes": [
      "The total is within 2% (-1.1%), so the measured block is the baseline; the re-measure compares against it with --compare.",
      "The measured block is v2 of the script replaying the same raw pages as v1 (measured 2026-10-29T15:35:22Z), and no figure moved: the pages held no repeated job or pipeline id, so de-duplication removed nothing, and v1's updated_before bound (2026-11-05) lay after the measurement, so dropping it admits no extra pipeline. Package totals, queue wait and peak concurrency cover the nine packages only; fleet-ci has its own block.",
      "The recorded per-package figures sum to 8662, not 8816; the recorded total was not their sum, so the 154 min difference is unexplained.",
      "Per package the gaps run -1.4% to +5.8%, both ways, which fits a shifted window rather than lost jobs. Replaying the same cache with the window moved 12 h later (2026-09-29T12:00Z .. 2026-10-29T12:00Z) reproduces every recorded per-package figure within 0.6% except pagerankr (576.0 vs 566): the original was most likely a rolling 30 days ending around noon UTC on 2026-10-29, not whole UTC days.",
      "check/verify here sums jobs named check, verify, check:* and check-*; the original grouping is not recorded.",
      "Setup share (33-77% per job) needs job logs, not the listings, so the script does not measure it.",
      "Queue p90 recorded as 24 min is stored as 1440 s.",
      "fleet-ci did not exist on GitLab at measurement time (HTTP 404)."
